Here's another for the list of stupid deaths. This one happened in NH++
(or is it -- this week?). I've gotten 3.1 but haven't put it on my home
machine yet.

I was running a Valkyrie, and she was doing really well. Ring of conflict,
Soulthief, etc. She got to the castle level, levitated around to the back
door, and went in. In one of the inner rooms (where there are two facing
rooms off the main corridor, each with a couple dragons in them), she 
met her doom. Picked the lock on one of the doors, out comes a yellow dragon.
There is apparently an orange dragon behind it, as I see the message:

"The blast of sleep gas hits the yellow dragon - More - 
The blast of sleep gas hits you - More - ", etc.

Not being sleep resistant, the sleep gas put the valkyrie to sleep.
If the yellow dragon woke up first, the (unseen) orange dragon would
breathe and put it to sleep. If the valk woke up first, the (unseen)
dragon would breathe and put HER to sleep, thanks, no doubt, to the ring
of conflict. This kept up until the valkyrie
starved to death.


